SCOPE. The MIT license above covers the *pipeline code* in this repository only
— everything under pipeline/, tests/, and the configuration format.

It does NOT cover the Qur'anic text, the translations, or the fonts this
pipeline compiles, and it grants no rights over them. Those carry their own,
mostly narrower terms: several are non-commercial, attribution-required and
verbatim-only. ATTRIBUTION.md is canonical for what may be redistributed and
under what obligations, and config/sources.yaml records the terms per resource
(the `license` field, which is compiled into the database and its published
edition artifacts).

Permissively licensing the code therefore does not make the data it produces
redistributable. Check ATTRIBUTION.md before shipping any compiled database.
